{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_012YqAgbyafQ23EJZij3hJeY","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Let me analyze the project context carefully and propose the next task.\n\n## Step 1: Analyze Project Context\n\nThe project is **go-unix-utils** - an experiment in specification-driven development using classic Unix utilities as a test bed.\n\n## Step 2: Summarize Project State\n\n**Problem**: Classic Unix utilities lack formal specifications. Man pages omit edge cases, flag interactions, and exit-code contracts. This project derives formal specifications from C source code and generates Go implementations using an AI coding agent, verified by differential testing.\n\n**Architecture**:\n- `cmd/` - Go implementations of utilities\n- `pkg/testutils/` - Differential testing harness\n- `pkg/sys/` - Syscall abstractions (Darwin/Linux)\n\n\n- `pkg/format/` - Output formatting\n- `magefiles/` - Mage build targets\n- `docs/` - PRDs, use cases, test suites\n\n**Current State**: Specifications are complete for testutils, sys, format, and several utilities (ts, wc, cat, sponge, ls, du). Generated code exists at specific tags but the working branch focuses on specifications.\n\n**Current Release**: rel01.0 is in progress with the ts use case marked as in_progress on specs but code generation hasn't started yet. Looking at the implementation status, the working branch contains only specifications—the actual generated Go code lives at the generation-merged tags, not on the current branch.\n\nSince the constraint limits me to one task and I need to prioritize the earliest incomplete release, I should focus on generating code for cmd/ts first. However, cmd/ts depends on pkg/testutils for differential testing, and while that package's spec is complete, its code also isn't on the working branch yet. Given the dependency chain, I need to start with the foundational pkg/testutils before moving to cmd/ts. I'm realizing the core of pkg/testutils is a DiffTest struct that handles binary execution, comparison, reporting, and normalization hooks like TimestampNormalizer. Based on the naming convention, the primary implementation should go in difftest.go, with a separate normalize.go for the normalization helpers. But since the constitution requires splitting implementation and tests into separate tasks and I can only create one task right now, I need to focus on just the implementation files without the test coverage.\n\nLooking at the scope, the implementation should cover the DiffTest struct itself, the RunDiffTests function for executing and comparing binaries, the Normalize type for composition, TimestampNormalizer for handling time-based differences, and file-state comparison support. My rough estimate puts this around 170-210 lines total, which fits comfortably within the budget.\n\nSince the constraint requires splitting implementation and tests into separate tasks but I can only create one task, I'll focus on just the implementation without tests. Given that I'm limited to exactly one task, the pkg/testutils implementation is the most impactful choice to propose.\n\nLooking at the dependency ordering, pkg/testutils needs to come first since cmd/ts tests will depend on it. Even though cmd/ts implementation doesn't directly depend on the test utilities, the principle of building foundational libraries before their consumers means I should tackle pkg/testutils first.\n\nI'll propose the pkg/testutils implementation task covering the core differential testing harness requirements.\n\nFor the file structure, I need to follow the naming convention—the primary file should be named after the main exported type, so `difftest.go` for the DiffTest struct and RunDiffTests function, with `normalize.go` handling the Normalize type and timestamp normalization helpers.\n\nLooking at the design from the requirements, I'm mapping out the DiffTest struct with its fields like Args, Stdin, Env, ExpectedExitCode, and a slice of Normalize functions, plus the RunDiffTests function signature that takes a test binary and reference binary. I'm also noting the 10-second timeout default and support for file-based expectations, then starting to structure this as a task with the full YAML definition.\n\nNow I'm laying out the specific files I need to create—difftest.go for the core struct and execution logic, and normalize.go for the timestamp normalization and helper functions—along with the detailed requirements mapping that ties back to the product spec. prd001 R1.1-R1.4 and R5.1\"\n      - id: R2\n        text: \"Define Normalize function type (func([]byte) []byte) and FileExpectation struct with Path and ExpectedContent fields -- per prd001 R1.4 and R5.1\"\n      - id: R3\n        text: \"Implement RunDiffTests(t *testing.T, goBinary, refBinary string, tests []DiffTest) that runs each DiffTest as a named subtest via t.Run -- per prd001 R2.1, R2.4, R3.6\"\n      - id: R4\n        text: \"Execute each binary with identical args, stdin, and env; capture stdout, stderr, and exit code independently; impose a configurable timeout defaulting to 10 seconds; create a per-test temporary working directory when WorkDir is not specified -- per prd001 R2.2, R2.3, R2.5\"\n      - id: R5\n        text: \"Apply Normalize functions in order to both binaries' stdout and stderr before comparison; compare normalized stdout, stderr, and exit code byte-for-byte; report divergence with args, stdin (truncated to 256 bytes), both stdouts, both stderrs, and both exit codes -- per prd001 R3.1-R3.5\"\n      - id: R6\n        text: \"Implement TimestampNormalizer that replaces common strftime timestamp patterns (e.g. 'Feb 19 12:34:56') with a fixed placeholder string -- per prd001 R4.2\"\n      - id: R7\n        text: \"Implement Compose function...\"\n      - id: R8\n        text: \"Compare FileExpectation.ExpectedContent byte-for-byte against the file at FileExpectation.Path after both binaries exit; report divergence in the same format as stdout divergence -- per prd001 R5.2\"\n\nNow I'm looking at the design decisions, which specify that the primary file should be pkg/testutils/difftest.go with DiffTest as the main exported type, and the RunDiffTests function signature needs to match the requirements from prd001.\n\nEach test runs as a subtest using t.Run with the test name, or by index if no name is provided, so failures are clearly identifiable. The timeout is configurable through context with a 10-second default, enforced via exec.CommandContext. Normalizers are applied as a slice in order before comparison, and the WorkDir field lets each test specify its working directory, creating a temporary directory per test when not provided. Looking at the remaining acceptance criteria, I need to verify that the DiffTest implementation handles file content comparisons, enforces the 10-second timeout with clear messaging, and that the testutils package builds cleanly without linting issues. Let me also cross-check the struct fields against the PRD requirements to ensure Args, Stdin, Env, exit codes, and the normalization function are all properly accounted for.\n\nI'm realizing the DiffTest struct should include a Name field for the subtests since the test suite references named test cases, and I need to confirm whether the Normalize type is correctly defined as a function signature and whether FileExpectations properly captures the expected file content requirements.\n\nNow I'm estimating the line count across the files—difftest.go should handle the struct definitions, the main RunDiffTests function with its loop and execution logic, plus helper functions for running binaries and comparing outputs, which should total around 190-230 lines. For normalize.go, I'm starting to sketch out the package structure and imports.\n\nBuilding out the normalizer implementations, including the timestamp normalizer with regex replacement and a Compose function to chain multiple normalizers together, should add another 50-55 lines total. That puts us comfortably within the 250-350 line budget.\n\nI'm also refining the DiffTest struct definition—it needs to hold a slice of Normalize functions rather than a single one, since the requirements specify that normalizers must be composable and applied in sequence.\n\nLooking at the acceptance criteria, the RunDiffTests function signature should accept a test slice directly from a cmd/ package without requiring additional setup, and I need to add a Name field to DiffTest for proper subtest naming. I'm also considering whether timeout should be a field on DiffTest itself or a parameter to RunDiffTests, though the requirements suggest it should be configurable per invocation with a 10-second default.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":74452,"cache_read_input_tokens":13968,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":74452},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bfa1b51a-895a-4b4f-865b-a0405d1b0200","uuid":"16b9ebde-45a9-434c-af22-4f5781929536"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_012YqAgbyafQ23EJZij3hJeY","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Step 1: Analyze Project Context\n\nAll information is available inline. No file reading needed.\n\n## Step 2: Project State Summary\n\n**Problem**: Classic Unix utilities lack formal specifications accessible to implementers. This project derives formal specs from C source, generates Go implementations via AI, and verifies them by differential testing against Homebrew GNU reference binaries.\n\n**Architecture**: Four stages — extract (C source) → specify (PRD + use case via human operator) → synthesize (mage-claude-orchestrator generates Go) → verify (pkg/testutils differential harness). Key packages: `pkg/testutils` (harness), `pkg/sys` (syscall abstractions), `pkg/format` (output formatting), `cmd/` (utility implementations).\n\n**Current state**: Working branch contains specifications only. Generated code lives at generation-merged git tags (not on current branch). All specs through rel02.1 are written. No Go code exists on the working branch for any package.\n\n**Current release**: `rel01.0` — ts specification and differential test (status: in_progress). One use case: `rel01.0-uc001-ts`, codestatus: not started.\n\n## Step 3: Priority Reasoning\n\nEarliest incomplete release is **rel01.0**. The dependency chain is:\n1. `pkg/testutils` — foundational harness; every `cmd/` test depends on it (P5: libraries before consumers)\n2. `cmd/ts` implementation — the rel01.0 deliverable\n3. `cmd/ts` tests — uses pkg/testutils\n\nWith 1-task limit and the split rule (implementation ≠ tests), the correct first task is **`pkg/testutils` implementation** (prd001-testutils R1–R5). This unblocks all downstream cmd/ test tasks.\n\n## Step 4: Task Proposal\n\n```yaml\n- index: 0\n  title: \"Implement pkg/testutils differential testing harness (prd001 R1-R5)\"\n  dependency: -1\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/specs/product-requirements/prd001-testutils.yaml (all requirements R1-R5 and acceptance criteria)\n      - docs/ARCHITECTURE.yaml (pkg/testutils component section)\n      - go.mod (module path: github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils)\n\n    files:\n      - path: pkg/testutils/difftest.go\n        action: create\n        note: DiffTest struct, FileExpectation struct, Normalize type, RunDiffTests function, binary execution and comparison logic\n      - path: pkg/testutils/normalize.go\n        action: create\n        note: TimestampNormalizer implementation and Compose helper for chaining normalizers\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: \"Define the Normalize function type as func([]byte) []byte per prd001 R1.4. Define the FileExpectation struct with fields Path (string) and ExpectedContent ([]byte) per prd001 R5.1.\"\n      - id: R2\n        text: \"Define the DiffTest struct with fields: Name (string), Args ([]string), Stdin ([]byte, nil means no stdin/EOF immediately), Env ([]string, nil means inherit test process environment), ExpectedExitCode (int), Normalize ([]Normalize, nil or empty means no normalization), WorkDir (string, empty means create per-test temp dir), and FileExpectations ([]FileExpectation) -- per prd001 R1.1-R1.4 and R5.1.\"\n      - id: R3\n        text: \"Implement RunDiffTests(t *testing.T, goBinary, refBinary string, tests []DiffTest) that iterates tests and runs each as a named subtest via t.Run using DiffTest.Name as the subtest label -- per prd001 R2.1, R3.6, AC1.\"\n      - id: R4\n        text: \"Within each subtest, execute both binaries with identical Args, Stdin, and Env; capture stdout, stderr, and exit code independently; when WorkDir is empty create a temp directory via t.TempDir() for both binaries; impose a timeout defaulting to 10 seconds per binary invocation using exec.CommandContext; fail with a clear timeout message if either binary exceeds the timeout -- per prd001 R2.2, R2.3, R2.5, AC5.\"\n      - id: R5\n        text: \"Apply all DiffTest.Normalize functions in order to both binaries' stdout and stderr before comparison; compare normalized stdout byte-for-byte; compare normalized stderr byte-for-byte; compare exit codes exactly; produce no output on a passing test; on any divergence call t.Errorf with: the args, stdin truncated to 256 bytes, reference stdout, Go stdout, reference stderr, Go stderr, and both exit codes -- per prd001 R3.1-R3.5, AC2.\"\n      - id: R6\n        text: \"After both binaries exit, for each FileExpectation read the file at FileExpectation.Path relative to WorkDir and compare its content to FileExpectation.ExpectedContent byte-for-byte; report divergence in the same format as stdout divergence -- per prd001 R5.2, AC4.\"\n      - id: R7\n        text: \"Implement TimestampNormalizer as a Normalize function that replaces common strftime timestamp patterns (matching strings like 'Feb 19 12:34:56' -- month abbreviation, day, HH:MM:SS) with a fixed placeholder string (e.g. 'TIMESTAMP') so that ts differential tests pass despite wall-clock differences -- per prd001 R4.2, AC3.\"\n      - id: R8\n        text: \"Implement Compose(normalizers ...Normalize) Normalize that returns a single Normalize function applying each normalizer in order to the input; when the slice is nil or empty return a no-op normalizer that returns the input unchanged -- per prd001 R4.3.\"\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: \"Primary source file is pkg/testutils/difftest.go, not testutils.go; the primary exported type is DiffTest per the project file-naming convention (primary source file is named after the primary exported type).\"\n      - id: D2\n        text: \"RunDiffTests signature is RunDiffTests(t *testing.T, goBinary, refBinary string, tests []DiffTest) with no timeout parameter; timeout is controlled by the default 10-second per-invocation limit per prd001 AC1 and R2.3.\"\n      - id: D3\n        text: \"DiffTest.Normalize is a []Normalize slice (not a single function) so that RunDiffTests applies them in order before comparison per prd001 R4.3; Compose converts a variadic list into a single chained Normalize.\"\n      - id: D4\n        text: \"Use exec.CommandContext with a context.WithTimeout to enforce the 10-second binary timeout; on timeout the subtest must fail with a message identifying the binary and that it timed out per prd001 R2.3, AC5.\"\n      - id: D5\n        text: \"WorkDir on DiffTest is an empty string by default; RunDiffTests calls t.TempDir() when WorkDir is empty to create an isolated per-test working directory for both binaries per prd001 R2.5.\"\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: \"A cmd/ package can define a []DiffTest slice and call RunDiffTests(t, goBinary, refBinary, tests) from a TestXxx function with no other setup -- per prd001 AC1.\"\n      - id: AC2\n        text: \"A passing test run produces no output to t; a failing test prints triggering args, stdin truncated to 256 bytes, both stdouts, both stderrs, and both exit codes -- per prd001 AC2.\"\n      - id: AC3\n        text: \"TimestampNormalizer applied to a string containing 'Feb 19 12:34:56' replaces the timestamp pattern with a fixed placeholder; two strings with different wall-clock timestamps but identical content otherwise compare equal after normalization -- per prd001 AC3.\"\n      - id: AC4\n        text: \"A DiffTest with a FileExpectation whose ExpectedContent differs from the actual file content causes RunDiffTests to call t.Errorf with the file path, expected content, and actual content -- per prd001 AC4.\"\n      - id: AC5\n        text: \"A DiffTest whose binary hangs fails within 10 seconds with a timeout error message rather than blocking the test run -- per prd001 AC5.\"\n      - id: AC6\n        text: \"go build ./pkg/testutils/... completes with no errors; golangci-lint ./pkg/testutils/... reports no warnings -- per prd001 AC6.\"\n```"}],"